To plot a curve in **PGFPlots** using the y-coordinates provided in a file (where each y-coordinate is on a new line) and increment x-coordinates sequentially for each line in the file, you can achieve this using a loop in LaTeX. Here's how:

Assume the file `data` is structured like this:
```
1.2
2.3
3.1
4.6
```

This means only y-coordinates are available, and the x-coordinates should increment automatically (starting at 0).

Here is the LaTeX code to create the plot:

```latex
\documentclass{standalone}
\usepackage{pgfplots}
\usepgfplotslibrary{external}
\tikzexternalize

\begin{document}

\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[
    grid=major,
    xlabel={$x$},
    ylabel={$y$},
    title={Plot from File "data"}
]
    % Generate coordinates by reading the file
    \pgfplotstableread[col sep=space, row sep=newline]{data}\datatable
    \addplot[
        mark=*,
        only marks
    ] table [x expr=\coordindex, y index=0] {\datatable};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}

\end{documet회원

